# Fake News Detection with Classic Machine Learning

**Can a model tell a real news article from a fake one just by reading the text?**

Fake news spreads fast, and nobody can fact-check every article by hand. This notebook tries a straightforward approach: turn each article into numbers using word counts, then train five familiar classifiers to decide whether it is *fake* or *real*, and compare how they do.

